  "stem": "A particle of mass m is moving in a straight line with momentum p. Starting at time t = 0, a force F = kt acts in the same direction on the moving particle during time interval T so that its momentum changes from p to 3p. Here k is a constant. The value of T is:",
  "options": {
    "A": "$2\\sqrt{\\frac{p}{k}}$",
    "B": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{2p}{k}}$",
    "C": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{2k}{p}}$",
    "D": "$2\\sqrt{\\frac{k}{p}}$"
  },
  "answer": {
    "keys": [
      "A"
    ]
  },
